{%- comment -%}
  Snippet: filter-drawer
  Phase 3, Stage 6. Mobile collection-filter drawer. Reuses the theme's
  existing overlay-drawer infrastructure (assets/theme.js openDrawer/
  closeDrawer — body-scroll locking, Escape-to-close, focus restore — and
  assets/theme.css section 11's shared drawer base) rather than a separate
  drawer system; only .filter-drawer/__overlay/__panel are added to those
  shared selector groups.

  Renders snippets/collection-filters.liquid a second time with
  id_prefix: 'Mobile' so every form/input id is distinct from the desktop
  rail's FacetFilterForm-Desktop instance (sections/collection-grid.liquid)
  while sharing identical field names/values — Stage 5's snippet already
  accepts id_prefix, so nothing about its filtering logic changes here.

  Params:
    collection - required, the current collection object
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="filter-drawer" id="FilterDrawer" data-filter-drawer aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="filter-drawer__overlay" data-filter-drawer-close></div>
  <div class="filter-drawer__panel" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="{{ 'filter_drawer.heading' | t }}">
    <div class="filter-drawer__header">
      <h2 class="filter-drawer__title">{{ 'filter_drawer.heading' | t }}</h2>
      <button type="button" class="icon-close-btn icon-close-btn--circle" data-filter-drawer-close aria-label="{{ 'general.close' | t }}">
        {%- render 'icon', icon: 'close' -%}
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class="filter-drawer__body">
      {%- render 'collection-filters', collection: collection, id_prefix: 'Mobile' -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
